<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brunei Shell Petroleum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as British Malayan Petroleum Company</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brunei Shell Petroleum is the main oil and gas producer of Brunei, jointly owned by the government of Brunei and the Shell group. As the British Malayan Petroleum Company, a Shell subsidiary, it discovered oil at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seria">Seria</a> in 1929, which transformed the small sultanate into one of the richest states in South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. It took its present name in 1957 and later became a joint venture with the state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brunei-shell-petroleum.jpg" alt="Brunei Shell Petroleum" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pangalau · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brunei_Shell_Petroleum_Head_Office_in_2025_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
